Miadi DeepDiver — user setup
===========================
Installed CLI: /usr/bin/deepdiver, private Python venv, pinned fork and wheels.
Provenance: /usr/share/miadi-deepdiver/SOURCE.json (not PyPI deepdiver 0.1.1).

As the desktop user, not root:
  miadi-deepdiver setup --claude
  miadi-deepdiver doctor --offline --claude
  deepdiver chrome launch
  # SIGN-IN NEEDED: a human signs in to their own Google account in this window.
  deepdiver chrome status
  miadi-deepdiver doctor --claude

Claude Code is installed/authenticated separately. setup --claude installs the
existing miadi-deepdiver@miadi-orchestration-kit marketplace plugin and the
fork's embedded skills with deepdiver skills install --agent claude. Existing
config, disabled plugin settings and differing personal skills are preserved.
Restart Claude to load plugin hooks. The kit's screenwalk-notebook skill and
plan-before-render gate stay canonical; read the fork manual with
  deepdiver skills show notebooklm-automation

setup alone does not launch Chrome or sign in. Config is mode 600 and only
created if absent; ~/.chrome-deepdiver is persistent. No maintainer script
writes a user's home. Removal/purge never remove profiles, credentials, skills
or config. Doctor does not print config values, page URLs or credentials.

Supported: amd64 Ubuntu 22.04 (Python 3.10), Debian 12 (3.11), Ubuntu 24.04
(3.12). Python 3.13+, arm64 and Termux are not packaged by this release.
Ubuntu's chromium-browser is a snap transition, so Playwright's exact captured
Chrome for Testing + headless shell is private under /usr/lib/miadi-deepdiver.
It does not replace your normal browser or download anything at install time.
The browser has its own upstream terms; see the browser package copyright.

CDP binds 127.0.0.1:9222, with no remote-debugging wildcard. Local users can
reach CDP: do not expose it, forward it to other hosts or reuse a sensitive
personal browsing profile. No --no-sandbox is installed. Chromium's standard
root-owned setuid sandbox is retained for hosts restricting user namespaces.
If a hardened kernel/AppArmor/container disallows both sandbox mechanisms,
report BLOCKED rather than disabling sandboxing. DISPLAY/XAUTHORITY must name
a reachable X desktop. A Wayland-only session requires XWayland; SSH-only
machines can run offline headless tests, but a person still needs a desktop
for sign-in. A headless test is not proof of Google sign-in or NotebookLM E2E.

  miadi-deepdiver doctor --offline --browser-smoke

Browser versions are deliberately pinned, not silently updated. Maintainers
must refresh source/dependency/browser locks, review security updates, bump
Debian versions and rebuild/retest/release. Upgrades rebuild only the private
venv from hash-verified packaged wheels, with --no-index and no system pip.
